executionContract.intendedBehavior:
On a Windows host, RuntimeSelectionPolicy.profile(basePath) also honors a PROTECTED profile record that was stored under another spelling of the same folder: a local spelling, opened later through a subst or mapped drive letter, a share or a device path.
The lookup runs when project.json does not declare verified-local and this spelling's own record is ABSENT or LEGACY. It lists the IDE store's records. A record counts when all of these hold:
- it is a strict version-1 'protected' record under its own file name;
- its project is a plain local drive path;
- that path has this folder's name (any name when this spelling is a root);
- Files.isSameFile says it is this folder.
A match pins PROTECTED for the session and asks the downgrade question. A confirmed downgrade writes 'legacy' under this spelling and under every matched record.
These behave as before: POSIX hosts, verified-local reads, and spellings whose own record is PROTECTED or UNTRUSTED. Any failure in the lookup matches nothing.
